Omega Healthcare Investors, Inc. is based in Hunt Valley, United States. The firm is incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew P. Gourmand CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 69 people. Revenue per employee of $17.2M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $11.6M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $640K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Omega Healthcare Investors, Inc is a large-cap real estate business with a $15.0B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $798M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 67 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 135% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3496451428301481},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 48% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PEB or OHI: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029696/peb-or-ohi-which-is-the-better-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3029696","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(OHI) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/OHI_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_111226083802_1794533882.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794533882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"compa